---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { PUBLIC_APP_NAME, PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL } from 'astro:env/client';
---

<Doc
  title={`Support | ${PUBLIC_APP_NAME}`}
  description={`Help with ${PUBLIC_APP_NAME}, answers to common questions, and how to report a drawing.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} is an async drawing game that lives inside
      iMessage. Draw a word, send it, and let your friend guess whenever
      they pick up their phone.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>How do I install it?</h3>
    <p>
      Open a Messages thread, tap the App Store icon in the iMessage app
      drawer, search for {PUBLIC_APP_NAME}, and tap it to enable the
      game inside iMessage.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I play?</h3>
    <p>
      Open {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} from the app drawer in any Messages thread,
      draw the prompt you are given, and send it back into the
      conversation for the other player to guess.
    </p>

    <h3>Why didn't my drawing send?</h3>
    <p>
      iMessage has to be on and online for the game to reach your
      friend, so check Settings, Messages, and your signal before trying
      again.
    </p>

    <h3>Where did my purchased pack go?</h3>
    <p>
      Open the pack screen inside {PUBLIC_APP_NAME} and tap Restore
      Purchases, then confirm under Settings, Apple ID, Subscriptions
      that you are signed in with the Apple ID that bought the pack.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I report a drawing?</h3>
    <p>Tap Report on the drawing and a pre-filled email opens for you to send.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="doc__aside">
    Data practices are covered in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    Still stuck? Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>
